@host = http://localhost:5080

### Health: liveness (process up) vs readiness (can serve traffic)  [concept 4]
GET {{host}}/health/live

###
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### Cache-aside: first call "database", second call "cache"  [concept 5]
GET {{host}}/products/1

###
GET {{host}}/products/1

### Update price -> cache key removed -> next GET reads the database again
PUT {{host}}/products/1/price
Content-Type: application/json

1299

### Output cache: generatedAt stays the same for 30 seconds  [concept 5/6]
GET {{host}}/catalog

### Rate limit: send this 7+ times quickly -> 429 with Retry-After  [concept 19]
GET {{host}}/search?q=phone

### Place an order with an idempotency key  [concepts 21, 12, 15]
# Send it twice: the second response has "replayed": true and no second order/charge.
# Watch the console: the background worker sends the email (with retries) after the response.
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 3f1c2a9e-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 2, "customerId": "asha" }

### Missing key -> 400
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 1, "customerId": "ravi" }

### Cursor pagination  [concept 14]
GET {{host}}/orders?limit=2

###
GET {{host}}/orders?after=2&limit=2

### Server-side timeout -> 504 after 2 s (run WITHOUT the debugger)  [concept 20]
GET {{host}}/slow-report

### Correlation id is echoed back; it appears in every log line for this request  [concept 22]
GET {{host}}/products/2
X-Correlation-Id: my-trace-123
